.Dd June 14, 2026
.Dt MBT_BITMAP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_bitmap_new ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_new_bits ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_fromarray ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_unref ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_unrefp ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_bits ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_bytes ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_raw ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_set ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_isset ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_clear ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_count ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_full ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_first_clear ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_first_set ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_union ,
.Nm mbt_bitmap_intersection
.Nd reference-counted bit-accurate bitmap
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/bitmap.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_bitmap_new "struct mbt_bitmap **out" "size_t sz"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_bitmap_new_bits "struct mbt_bitmap **out" "size_t nbits"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_bitmap_fromarray "struct mbt_bitmap **out" "uint8_t *buf" "size_t len" "size_t nbits"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_bitmap_unref "struct mbt_bitmap *tb"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_bitmap_unrefp "struct mbt_bitmap **tb"
.Ft size_t
.Fn mbt_bitmap_bits "struct mbt_bitmap *tb"
.Ft size_t
.Fn mbt_bitmap_bytes "struct mbt_bitmap *tb"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_bitmap_raw "struct mbt_bitmap *tb" "void *out" "size_t len"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_bitmap_set "struct mbt_bitmap *tb" "size_t bit"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_bitmap_isset "struct mbt_bitmap *tb" "size_t bit"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_bitmap_clear "struct mbt_bitmap *tb"
.Ft size_t
.Fn mbt_bitmap_count "struct mbt_bitmap *tb"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_bitmap_full "struct mbt_bitmap *tb"
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn mbt_bitmap_first_clear "struct mbt_bitmap *tb"
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn mbt_bitmap_first_set "struct mbt_bitmap *tb"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_bitmap_union "struct mbt_bitmap *a" "struct mbt_bitmap *b" "struct mbt_bitmap *out"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_bitmap_intersection "struct mbt_bitmap *a" "struct mbt_bitmap *b" "struct mbt_bitmap *out"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A reference-counted bitmap used for tracking piece availability
in torrents and peer bitfields.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_bitmap_new
allocates a bitmap with
.Fa sz
bytes of storage.
.Fn mbt_bitmap_new_bits
allocates a bitmap sized for exactly
.Fa nbits
bits (rounded up to whole bytes).
.Fn mbt_bitmap_fromarray
creates a bitmap from an existing byte array, capping at
.Fa nbits .
.Pp
.Fn mbt_bitmap_unref
decrements the reference count, freeing the bitmap when it reaches zero.
.Fn mbt_bitmap_unrefp
is a cleanup helper taking a pointer-to-pointer.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_bitmap_set
sets bit
.Fa bit
(returns 0 on success, negative on out of bounds).
.Fn mbt_bitmap_isset
returns 1 if set, 0 if clear, negative on out of bounds.
.Fn mbt_bitmap_clear
clears all bits.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_bitmap_count
returns the number of set bits.
.Fn mbt_bitmap_full
returns 1 if all bits are set.
.Fn mbt_bitmap_first_clear
returns the index of the first unset bit, or \-1.
.Fn mbt_bitmap_first_set
returns the index of the first set bit, or \-1.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_bitmap_bits
returns the total number of bits.
.Fn mbt_bitmap_bytes
returns the byte size of the backing storage.
.Fn mbt_bitmap_raw
copies the raw bytes into
.Fa out .
.Pp
.Fn mbt_bitmap_union
and
.Fn mbt_bitmap_intersection
compute set operations, writing the result into
.Fa out .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt 3 ,
.Xr mbt_torrent 3 ,
.Xr mbt_peer 3
